WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.700
We all have seen raisins swelling up when

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.120
kept in water for some time.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.430
Any idea how this magic works?

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.140
Well, it is simply the process of osmosis

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:17.180
which results in the swelling of these resins!

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.360
You heard me right.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.715
It is Osmosis process due to which the water

00:00:21.715 --> 00:00:24.070
from the surrounding medium enters the cells

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.680
of raisins helping them to swell.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.450
Can we define osmosis once?

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.751
It is simply defined as the process in which

00:00:32.751 --> 00:00:35.000
water moves from higher water concentration

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.280
to lower water concentration through a semi

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.600
permeable membrane.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.860
An interesting thing to know about osmosis

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.300
is that the movement of water is affected

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.340
by the amount of a substances dissolved in it!

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.600
And what does this mean exactly?

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.219
Let us conduct an experiment to understand it better.

00:00:55.219 --> 00:00:57.640
Let us take three plates or containers with

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.949
salt solutions of different concentration

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:00.949
in each.

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:06.390
Let us add a few red blood cells that is RBCs in each.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.917
After a while we clearly notice that the first

00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:10.730
set has cells which are shrinked.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.328
The second set has cells that are just the

00:01:13.328 --> 00:01:16.050
same while the third set has cells which are

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.450
swollen or bulged.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.160
Any idea why this happened?

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.210
Let us understand this.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.979
In the first case, the water content in the

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:27.620
surrounding solution was less as compared

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.830
to the cells placed in it.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:32.781
In other words, the salt content of the solution

00:01:32.781 --> 00:01:36.040
is more and therefore this solution is a concentrated

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:36.720
one.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.660
That is the reason why the water molecules

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:41.920
moved from inside the cells to the outside

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.880
solution as the concentration of water was

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.980
higher within the cells.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.900
Hence the cells started shrinking.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.420
This kind of a solution is called as a HYPERTONIC

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.240
solution.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:57.180
That is the solution with higher salt concentration.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.420
Now let’s have a look at the second case.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.439
Here, the level of salt and water seems to

00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:06.950
be the same on either side of the cell membranes.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.819
That is both, within and outside the cell.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.720
Therefore there was a balance in the movement

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.480
of water.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.860
What do we understand by this?

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.760
It means that the movement of water was the

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.579
same in either directions.

00:02:21.579 --> 00:02:25.230
As a result, the size of the cell did not change.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.340
It remained the same!

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:30.420
Do you know what such a solution is called as?

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.499
It is called an ISOTONIC solution.

00:02:32.499 --> 00:02:36.034
The two solutions are isotonic when the concentration

00:02:36.034 --> 00:02:38.969
of water is same on either sides of the semi

00:02:38.969 --> 00:02:41.349
permeable membrane!

00:02:41.349 --> 00:02:43.799
Now let us focus on this third set.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.800
The cells in this case are surrounded by a

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.080
dilute solution that is by higher water concentration.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:54.290
The salt dissolved is less and the water content

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.120
is higher.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.180
Therefore, water molecules move inside the

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.860
cells and hence the cells got swollen.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:05.700
Such a solution is called as a HYPOTONIC solution.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.380
In other words, solution with a higher water

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:11.400
concentration compared to the other.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.940
This is how various solutions and their different

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.980
concentrations help cells to sustain pressure

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.959
and to survive.

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:22.066
Movement of molecules across the plasma membrane

00:03:22.066 --> 00:03:24.719
is also influenced by this simple process

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:25.659
of osmosis!

